// Pull request: #6637 New Rule: Arbitrary File Copy Via Dtutil.EXE
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6637
// Pull request author: COMPUMAX-EC
// Change: new rule
// Title: Arbitrary File Copy Via Dtutil.EXE
// Sigma ID: 33171905-1775-497b-a2c6-4d22bec061d4
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Geovanny Basantes
// Date: 2026-11-04 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1105, stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects the use of "dtutil.exe" (SQL Server Integration Services package management utility) to
//   copy a file that is not an SSIS package (.dtsx). Adversaries can abuse dtutil's "/COPY FILE;"
//   option to copy arbitrary files, such as payloads or tools, to another location using a signed
//   Microsoft binary.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administrative use of dtutil to copy SSIS packages saved with a non-standard extension
// References:
//   - https://github.com/LOLBAS-Project/LOLBAS/blob/a79893e7ad7fe69e9eeb37c82e90685e10663312/yml/OtherMSBinaries/Dtutil.yml
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/integration-services/dtutil-utility
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/c489e769d20bca9d6340d9f2b4ba0b7910c148dc/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_dtutil_file_copy.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\dtutil.exe" and ((ProcessCommandLine contains "-copy" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/copy" or ProcessCommandLine contains "–copy" or ProcessCommandLine contains "—copy" or ProcessCommandLine contains "―copy") and ProcessCommandLine contains "file;")) and (not(ProcessCommandLine matches regex "(?i)file;(\"[^\"]+\\.dtsx\"|[^\\s\"]+\\.dtsx(\\s|$))"))
